// Title: Suspicious Redirection to Local Admin Share
// Sigma ID: ab9e3b40-0c85-4ba1-aede-455d226fd124
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-01-16 | Modified: 2023-12-28
// ATT&CK: exfiltration, T1048
// Description: Detects a suspicious output redirection to the local admins share, this technique is often found
//   in malicious scripts or hacktool stagers
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://www.microsoft.com/security/blog/2022/01/15/destructive-malware-targeting-ukrainian-organizations/
//   - http://blog.talosintelligence.com/2022/09/lazarus-three-rats.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_susp_redirect_local_admin_share.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains ">" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "\\\\127.0.0.1\\admin$\\" or ProcessCommandLine contains "\\\\localhost\\admin$\\")
